The general-SQL core of this grammar (expression precedence, SELECT, CTEs, joins,
window functions, and the surrounding tooling scaffold) derives from that project.
The T-SQL-specific surface — the SSMS header, bracketed parameterized types, IF/WHILE
control flow, TRY/CATCH, cursors, table hints, and the rest of T-SQL's distinguishing
constructs — is original work added on top of that base.
